Article Summary : 


Will AI kill the $963 billion ad agency industry?

From an interesting article - Big tech's AI ad tools rattle agencies. So let me summarize what I learnt.

Not yet, but they will need to reinvent themselves to stay relevant. 

With tools from Google's AI Max Research campaigns and Demand Chat, to emerging agentic AI across Google Ads and Anaytics - Media buying is fast and frictionless!

So the real question -
Could AI kill this well established agency model?

Algorithmic efficiency does kill the most fundamental part of marketing campaigns. Differentiation.

COO and Co-founder of TheSmallBigIdea Manish Solanki mentions that marketing is rapidly inclining towards an analytical approach.

But, the real win stands in creativity and cultural relevance. You have to move up the value chain. Now, the edge lies not with access to AI, but how you orchestrate your campaign.
Think stronger brand creatives. Be an invaluable brand partner and help brands to decide the perfect mix and execute strategies with the tools at hand. 

There is no need to panic.
AI will generate options through its trained patterns, but the compelling story, emotional and strategic depth to a campaign and the final curatorial judgement, is always fundamentally human. Because the best stories are often what you heard from someone and not something.

Bottom line is you'll have to work with AI and not against it to reach marketing outcomes. Tell your story and keep it relevant, and re-invent. Faster. Better.